1
00:00:00,299 --> 00:00:03,584
If you want to deploy a cluster, start with Deploy a Cluster.

2
00:00:03,925 --> 00:00:06,165
You do not need to search through script names.

3
00:00:06,528 --> 00:00:11,221
Start Here offers four choices: deploy, configure an existing cluster,

4
00:00:11,520 --> 00:00:14,722
monitor and verify, or run saved automation.

5
00:00:15,064 --> 00:00:18,670
This series follows the current console with simulated examples.

6
00:00:18,904 --> 00:00:21,834
It does not execute changes against a real environment.

7
00:00:22,147 --> 00:00:24,720
Open Overview for the daily operations view.

8
00:00:25,031 --> 00:00:29,127
The four action cards open deployment, configuration, infrastructure

9
00:00:29,170 --> 00:00:30,620
recovery and monitoring.

10
00:00:30,919 --> 00:00:32,810
These links do not execute work.

11
00:00:33,180 --> 00:00:37,746
The summary now shows Managed clusters, Open review items, Running jobs and

12
00:00:37,788 --> 00:00:39,419
Fresh P E Good readbacks.

13
00:00:39,471 --> 00:00:43,055
Managed cluster counts come from explicitly registered records.

14
00:00:43,396 --> 00:00:47,194
They are not automatic discovery, and recovery profile counts remain a

15
00:00:47,236 --> 00:00:48,019
separate concept.

16
00:00:48,474 --> 00:00:51,319
Read the timestamp and evidence below each record.

17
00:00:51,690 --> 00:00:54,506
Refresh reloads saved operational records.

18
00:00:54,847 --> 00:00:58,730
Merely opening or refreshing this page never contacts Prism Element.

19
00:00:59,156 --> 00:01:03,508
Needs attention retains observed failed or interrupted jobs and P E

20
00:01:03,551 --> 00:01:04,584
observation issues.

21
00:01:04,934 --> 00:01:08,454
Open the original job or review the cluster before deciding what to do.

22
00:01:08,689 --> 00:01:12,173
A newer successful job does not erase an earlier failure record.

23
00:01:12,657 --> 00:01:16,923
Choose Update review, assign an owner, and record useful reconciliation

24
00:01:17,137 --> 00:01:18,425
notes without secrets.

25
00:01:18,732 --> 00:01:21,249
Acknowledge the item while follow-up is in progress.

26
00:01:21,633 --> 00:01:25,032
Choose Resolved after review only after checking the actual outcome.

27
00:01:25,260 --> 00:01:28,366
Acknowledgement and resolution update the review record.

28
00:01:28,784 --> 00:01:33,050
They do not fix the target, approve execution, change recovery gates or

29
00:01:33,093 --> 00:01:34,053
replay a job.

30
00:01:34,330 --> 00:01:38,426
A new failed P E readback can reopen a resolved observation item.

31
00:01:38,682 --> 00:01:42,234
Open Clusters to add or edit an explicit managed record.

32
00:01:42,542 --> 00:01:46,980
Link its saved configuration files, pipeline and recovery profile, then

33
00:01:47,065 --> 00:01:50,948
enter the expected cluster identity, complete node baseline and credential

34
00:01:51,161 --> 00:01:51,859
reference.

35
00:01:52,215 --> 00:01:56,737
Importing expected membership from Foundation Y A M L does not discover the

36
00:01:56,780 --> 00:01:57,591
actual target.

37
00:01:58,017 --> 00:02:01,858
Stale observation means the stored P E evidence is older than fifteen

38
00:02:01,943 --> 00:02:04,319
minutes or is unavailable as fresh evidence.

39
00:02:04,689 --> 00:02:07,441
It does not by itself mean the cluster is unhealthy.

40
00:02:07,761 --> 00:02:12,326
Select Review for the cluster, then Collect P E health, read-only, to

41
00:02:12,369 --> 00:02:13,358
request new evidence.

42
00:02:13,886 --> 00:02:18,920
Collection requires expected U U I D, node baseline, a credential reference

43
00:02:19,133 --> 00:02:21,395
and trusted H T T P S.

44
00:02:21,694 --> 00:02:23,955
Missing or failed evidence stays unknown.

45
00:02:24,254 --> 00:02:28,520
P E reported health is narrower than N C C, resilience testing and

46
00:02:28,563 --> 00:02:29,870
application acceptance.

47
00:02:30,152 --> 00:02:33,736
Existing recovery profiles remain listed separately on Clusters.

48
00:02:34,163 --> 00:02:37,192
The streamlined sidebar keeps ordinary tasks visible.

49
00:02:37,448 --> 00:02:41,971
Expand Advanced Automation for workflows, scripts, configuration files,

50
00:02:42,184 --> 00:02:44,156
schedules and execution history.

51
00:02:44,507 --> 00:02:47,942
Optional Integrations contains the preview integration paths.

52
00:02:48,134 --> 00:02:52,400
Administration contains setup, credentials, appliance operations and

53
00:02:52,443 --> 00:02:53,168
settings.

54
00:02:53,510 --> 00:02:57,435
N K P Validation Evidence carries a Preview badge and retains its specialist

55
00:02:57,520 --> 00:02:58,062
sources.

56
00:02:58,433 --> 00:03:01,803
Use execution history and target readbacks for ordinary cluster

57
00:03:01,974 --> 00:03:02,714
verification.

58
00:03:03,339 --> 00:03:07,051
For a normal task, choose the correct workflow, review the saved

59
00:03:07,179 --> 00:03:11,958
configuration, run the available dry run, obtain any required approval, and

60
00:03:12,001 --> 00:03:12,880
submit once.

61
00:03:13,206 --> 00:03:15,318
Follow its record in Jobs and Queue.

62
00:03:15,552 --> 00:03:17,771
Investigate failures before retrying.

63
00:03:18,112 --> 00:03:21,718
You can retain Start Here or Overview as your browser landing preference.

64
00:03:21,952 --> 00:03:25,903
Part two follows cluster deployment through the Foundation V M workflow.
